# Subtitle

> Fuente: https://www.chartjs.org/docs/latest/configuration/subtitle.html
> Exportado: 2026-07-12 20:57 UTC

# [#](#subtitle) Subtitle

Subtitle is a second title placed under the main title, by default. It has exactly the same configuration options with the main [title](/docs/latest/configuration/title.html).

## [#](#subtitle-configuration) Subtitle Configuration

Namespace: `options.plugins.subtitle`. The global defaults for subtitle are configured in `Chart.defaults.plugins.subtitle`.

Exactly the same configuration options with [title](/docs/latest/configuration/title.html) are available for subtitle, the namespaces only differ.

## [#](#example-usage) Example Usage

The example below would enable a title of 'Custom Chart Subtitle' on the chart that is created.

```
const chart = new Chart(ctx, {
    type: 'line',
    data: data,
    options: {
        plugins: {
            subtitle: {
                display: true,
                text: 'Custom Chart Subtitle'
            }
        }
    }
});
```
